# PawShop PayPal credentials (Sandbox first, Live later).
#
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. It contains no secret, and it must never contain one:
# real values are injected by the deployment's secret manager and live only in
# /etc/pawshop/paypal.env (0600 root:root) on the host.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE
# commerce.env is a closed 20-key contract that the deployment validates with an
# exact key-set comparison (see _commerce/scripts/production-env-file.cjs). The
# startup preflight (ExecStartPre -> scripts/preflight-production-host.mjs) parses
# that file and rejects ANY extra field, so adding PAYPAL_* to commerce.env makes
# the commerce unit refuse to start — which takes the storefront API down with it,
# because one process serves both the shop and the admin. google-oauth.env and
# connector.env set the precedent for keeping unrelated secrets out of it.
#
# systemd reads this file as an OPTIONAL EnvironmentFile
# (`EnvironmentFile=-/etc/pawshop/paypal.env` in ops/commerce/pawshop-commerce.service).
# The leading `-` matters: a missing non-optional EnvironmentFile makes systemd
# refuse to start the unit outright. With no file present the payment module is
# simply not registered (production-modules.cjs adds it only when credentials
# exist), so an un-provisioned host keeps the framework default and NO provider
# is exposed to a customer-facing region.
#
# ALL SIX VALUES MUST BE PRESENT TOGETHER. production-policy.cjs refuses to start
# when only some of them are set (fail-closed), so a half-written file cannot
# silently leave the shop with a payment method that cannot take money.
#
# PAYPAL_SANDBOX must be the literal string "true" while testing against
# developer.paypal.com, and "false" together with Live credentials afterwards.
# PAYPAL_RETURN_URL / PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL must be absolute https URLs on the
# storefront origin, and must be plain paths with NO `#` fragment: PayPal appends
# `?token=...&PayerID=...` on return, and a fragment would push the query string
# out of window.location.search, breaking the return-detection in PawShop.html.

# --- credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PAYPAL_SANDBOX=true
# PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=WH-

# --- return path ------------------------------------------------------------
# PAYPAL_RETURN_URL=https://pawlivora.com/PawShop.html
# PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL=https://pawlivora.com/PawShop.html
